---
import CommercialLayout from '../../components/CommercialLayout.astro';
import CitabilityBlock from '../../components/CitabilityBlock.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const utm = Astro.url.searchParams.get('utm') || 'audit-page';
const canonical = `${SITE.url}/audit/`;

const FAQ = [
  {
    question: 'Is the inbound lead audit really free?',
    answer:
      'Yes, and there is no obligation afterwards. Scoping without seeing data is guesswork, and guesswork gets priced defensively, so the audit is as much for us as for you. You keep the written action list whether or not you hire us.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What do you need from us?',
    answer:
      'A read-only export of inbound records from the last full month, a look at your form and routing configuration, and forty-five minutes with someone who knows how leads actually get worked. We do not ask for admin access to production.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What does the audit actually measure?',
    answer:
      'Four counts, reconciled: requests that arrived, records created, records with a live owner, and records actually worked. The gaps between them are where revenue leaks, and they are rarely where the org chart suggests.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does it take?',
    answer:
      'One call of thirty to forty-five minutes, then three to five working days for the written findings. Longer only if the export needs work before it can be reconciled.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What if the answer is that we do not need you?',
    answer:
      'Then we say so. If the fix is a setting in software you already pay for, we name the setting. If your funnel converts fine and the constraint is traffic, no automation changes that arithmetic and you should know it early.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is this a sales call in disguise?',
    answer:
      'The output is a written list you keep. We do quote for implementation when it is warranted, and we take no commission from any tool we recommend, which is why the recommendation is sometimes to change nothing.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: FAQ.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.answer },
  })),
};
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Free Inbound Lead Audit: Scope and Output · OperStack"
  description="A free inbound lead audit: four reconciled counts, gaps ranked by what they cost, and a written action list you keep. No deck, no obligation."
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={faqSchema}
>
  <div class="wrap audit-wrap">
    <h1>Free inbound lead audit</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Forty-five minutes and a written action list. We reconcile what arrived against what
      actually got worked, rank the gaps by what they cost you, and name the two worth fixing
      first. No deck, no obligation, and you keep the list either way.
    </p>

    <CitabilityBlock
      text="OperStack runs a free inbound lead audit: four reconciled counts covering requests that arrived, records created, records with an owner, and records actually worked, with the gaps ranked by cost."
    />

    <h2>The four counts</h2>
    <p>
      Almost every inbound problem shows up as a gap between two of these. Teams usually know one
      of the numbers and assume the other three.
    </p>
    <ol class="numbers">
      <li><b>Arrived.</b> Requests submitted across every channel, including the ones that never reached a system.</li>
      <li><b>Created.</b> Records that exist in the CRM. The gap to arrived is a capture or integration failure.</li>
      <li><b>Owned.</b> Records with a live, correct owner. The gap here is almost always a routing rule with no fallback branch.</li>
      <li><b>Worked.</b> Records that received a real first response. The gap is coverage, capacity, or a queue nobody watches.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>The four counts for your last full month, reconciled, with each gap traced to one layer</li>
      <li>Findings ranked by the cost of the current failure, not by how easy they are to fix</li>
      <li>The two things to change first, and an explicit list of what not to bother with</li>
      <li>A build, buy, or configure call per finding, including when the answer is a setting you already own</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we need from you</h2>
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li>A read-only export of inbound records from the last full month</li>
      <li>A look at your form and routing configuration, screenshots are fine</li>
      <li>Forty-five minutes with someone who knows how leads actually get worked, not how the process is documented</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      We do not ask for admin access to production systems, and you should be sceptical of anyone
      who does at this stage.
    </p>

    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    <p>
      Not a maturity score. Scoring an organisation from one to five creates a gap and positions
      the scorer to fill it. Not a vendor shortlist either: we take no commission from any tool,
      which is why a recommendation is sometimes to change a setting rather than buy anything.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      If the honest finding is that your funnel converts adequately and the constraint is traffic,
      we will say that. It is a short call and it saves you a quarter.
    </p>

    <h2>After the audit</h2>
    <p>
      If something is worth building, it is quoted per module against
      <a href="/services/">the services</a> and priced on
      <a href="/pricing/">the pricing page</a>. The most common outcomes are
      <a href="/services/lead-routing-software/">lead routing setup</a>,
      <a href="/services/ai-automation-services/">AI automation services</a>, and
      <a href="/services/lead-management-system/">lead management system setup</a>.
      The method behind the audit itself is published in full in the
      <a href="/guides/inbound-lead-audit/">inbound lead audit guide</a>, and you are welcome to
      run it without us.
    </p>

    <h2>Request the audit</h2>

    <form id="audit-form" novalidate>
      <input type="hidden" name="source" value={`audit:${utm}`} />
      <div class="row">
        <div>
          <label for="name">Name *</label>
          <input id="name" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="phone">WhatsApp / Phone *</label>
          <input id="phone" name="phone" type="tel" required autocomplete="tel" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="email">Email</label>
        <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="message">What does your inbound look like today?</label>
        <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" placeholder="Site, CRM, team size, market..."></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="consent">
        <input type="checkbox" id="consent" name="consent" required />
        <label for="consent">I agree to be contacted about this audit request.</label>
      </div>
      <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
        <label for="website">Website</label>
        <input id="website" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn" id="submit">Request audit →</button>
      <p class="msg" id="form-msg" hidden></p>
    </form>

    <FaqSection items={FAQ} />
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ utm }}>
    const form = document.getElementById('audit-form');
    const msg = document.getElementById('form-msg');
    const btn = document.getElementById('submit');
    const loadedAt = Date.now();

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      msg.hidden = true;
      btn.disabled = true;
      const fd = new FormData(form);
      const payload = {
        name: fd.get('name'),
        phone: fd.get('phone'),
        email: fd.get('email'),
        message: fd.get('message'),
        source: fd.get('source') || `audit:${utm}`,
        website: fd.get('website'),
        formLoadedAt: loadedAt,
        formElapsedMs: Date.now() - loadedAt,
      };
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/lead/', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.error || 'Request failed');
        if (typeof window.operStackTrack === 'function') {
          window.operStackTrack('lead_form_submit', { form_name: 'audit', source: payload.source });
        }
        window.location.href = '/thanks/';
      } catch (err) {
        msg.textContent = err.message || 'Something went wrong. Email info@oper-stack.com';
        msg.className = 'msg err';
        msg.hidden = false;
        btn.disabled = false;
      }
    });
  </script>
</CommercialLayout>

<style>
  .audit-wrap { max-width: 720px; }
  .bullets { margin: 0 0 24px 20px; color: var(--muted); }
  .bullets li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .pricing-link {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  form {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 28px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid rgba(61, 184, 169, 0.22);
  }
  label { display: block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 6px; color: rgba(245, 242, 236, 0.9); }
  input, textarea {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
    color: var(--paper);
    font: inherit;
  }
  input:focus, textarea:focus {
    outline: 2px solid rgba(61, 184, 169, 0.45);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }
  .row { display: grid; gap: 16px; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  button:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; opacity: 0; height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
  .msg { font-size: 14px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .msg.err { color: #f5a962; }
  .consent { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .consent input { width: auto; margin-top: 3px; }
</style>
